# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Outlook Automation CRM — frontend ignore rules
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Dependencies ----------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit node_modules. Several dependencies here ship prebuilt native
# binaries chosen per platform (@rolldown/binding-*, @tailwindcss/oxide-*,
# lightningcss-*, @oxlint/binding-*). A tree committed from Windows carries the
# win32-x64-msvc bindings, and checking it out on a Linux build server leaves
# npm with an already-populated directory holding binaries it cannot execute.
# The lockfile is what makes installs reproducible — not the directory.
node_modules/
.pnp/
.pnp.js
.yarn/

# --- Environment & secrets -------------------------------------------------
# Every VITE_* value is inlined into the shipped bundle, so these are public by
# nature — but the file is still per-environment. `.env.example` is the tracked
# template, and `src/config/env.js` falls back to the same defaults.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Caches ----------------------------------------------------------------
.cache/
.npm/
.eslintcache
.oxlintcache

# --- Editors & IDEs --------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Operating system ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
